    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1323">

                <pb facs="1257" n="1091" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1091"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 151.07/84</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Chinese Minister
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 49</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State.</hi>
                            <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 1, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith for
                    your information and for such action as you may deem appropriate copy of a
                    letter of April 28, 1917, from the Secretary of War, transmitting the copy of a
                    telegram received from General Pershing, in regard to the Chinese refugees now
                    at Columbus, New Mexico.</p>
                <p>The Department will be glad to communicate to the War Department at an early date
                    your decision relative to this matter.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
